<title>NORWAY: Nycomed share up on takeover rumour.</title>
<headline>Nycomed share up on takeover rumour.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian drug company Nycomed ASA rose strongly on the Oslo Bourse on Tuesday on rumours it might be taken over by Roche Holding AG of Switzerland or an unnamed German pharmaceutical group, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it is only rumours but they have driven the share to be the winner of the day if you look at the percentage rise,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Nycomed A shares were up 7.10 percent at 83.00 crowns and B shares had increased 7.24 percent to 81.50 crowns shortly after noon (1000gmt).</p>
<p>Nycomed declined comment.</p>
<p>&quot;We as a principle don't comment on rumors of that kind,&quot; a Nycomed spokesman said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
